[{"result":{"data":{"json":{"id":"1356","stub":{"id":"1356","section":"1. Rock Hill to Oakland Valley","altname":"","river":"Neversink","difficulty":"IItoIV","states":["USA-NYO"]},"primaryGaugeStatus":{"status":"below-recommended","latestReading":{"value":"413","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:30:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"metric":"cfs","adjustedDifficulty":null},"pointOfInterests":[{"type":"put-in","description":null,"id":"112207","location":{"latitude":"41.632401","longitude":"-74.618301"},"name":"Put In","distance":"0","photoID":null,"difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false},{"type":"takeout","description":null,"id":"117489","location":{"latitude":"41.504501","longitude":"-74.647499"},"name":"Take Out","distance":"11","photoID":null,"difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false}],"alerts":[{"id":"101247932","title":null,"post_date":"2011-04-21 04:00:00+00","detail":"We had a tire slashed at the Cuddebackville/ Oakland Valley/Route 49 take out for the Neversink today. We were parked on the SE side (I think) near the bridge, well away from any no trespassing signs. There is NO DOUBT the tire was cut with a knife. This is an amazing section of river, but it isn't worth a $150 tire. This happened on 5/26/2012 so disregard the date on the post, cause I can't figure out how to add a new comment.","user":null}],"photos":[{"id":"39600","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"9024","description":"During an a scout at unboatable level","caption":"High falls","poi_name":"High falls","subject":"","author":"Jimmy D","poi_id":"102272","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/39600","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/39600"}},{"id":"877674","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"877945","description":"A drop of about 8', with a big, wide tongue. ","caption":"Denton Falls","poi_name":"Denton Falls","subject":"","author":"Steve McLuckie","poi_id":"102270","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/877674","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/877674"}},{"id":"877673","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"877944","description":"Typical scenery a mile or so below the Bridgeville put in. It's easy class 1 to 2- for the first couple of miles.","caption":"Neversink Scenery","poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"Steve McLuckie","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/877673","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/877673"}},{"id":"877676","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"877947","description":"One of many good spots between Denton Falls and High Falls.","caption":"","poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"Steve McLuckie","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/877676","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/877676"}},{"id":"877677","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"877948","description":"River left is a boof of 3 to 4 feet. Far river right has a narrow tongue up against the rocks, and hole taking up much of the center right. You may not want to be inthe hole.","caption":"Two Choices","poi_name":null,"subject":null,"author":"Steve McLuckie","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/877677","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/877677"}},{"id":"877675","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"877946","description":"In between Denton Falls and High Falls. Typical scenery, but calmer water than a lot of this 1 mile stretch.","caption":"Neversink Gorge","poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"Steve McLuckie","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/877675","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/877675"}},{"id":"877678","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"877949","description":"It looked like it could be sticky, but nobody found a sticky spot","caption":"Soft Landing","poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"Steve McLuckie","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/877678","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/877678"}}],"detail":{"id":"1356","permitUrl":"","permitInfo":"","description":"This 11.3 mile section of the Neversink is mostly class 1 to 2, but has about 1.5 miles of exciting  class 3 to 4 rapids about halfway through. There is a mostly unobtrusive quarry operation along the right for the first 1.5 miles, but  the gorge is very remote and isolated from there until the first houses appear on river right about 1/2 mile before the takeout in Oakland Valley\n\nLat/longitude coords are very close, from TopoZone and Google Maps. Thanks to Adam, from the Northeast Paddlers' Message Board for most of this information:\n\nThere are two major drops on the Neversink. Denton Falls is a slide run straight down the middle with no holes at the bottom. High Falls is small vertical drop of 5 feet, easily run far river right, or by taking the boof left of the rocky island. After High Falls is about 4 miles of flat to class 2 rapids. In between Denton and High Falls is the Gorge section, which is class 3-4 depending on levels. Over 7.5, I would say it is a 4. Lots of holes, waves and sticky spots. At bottom of the gorge, there are some waves to surf at 6 - 7 feet, above that they become pretty sticky. The river is not a great play river, with only a handful of waves on the 6-8 miles. However, it is beautiful and absolutely desolate. Have seen bald eagles every time I've been down. (Note- at 750 don't recall much play, but at 1200 there was a fair amount. Nothing amazing, but enough waves, pour overs and squirt spots to keep the easier section interesting. Still, bring your longest boat).\n\nThe put-in is just outside the gates to Holiday Mtn. Ski area off of Bridgeville Rd (public fishing access). The usual take-out is at the Oakland Valley bridge on county route 49. Alternate take outs further downstream include a small pullout about 1.5 miles south on route 49 or at  the D&H Canal museum, just off of route 209 in Huguenot NY.\n\nHere's a Google map showing the river, along with the main rapids, put in and takeout locations, and the shuttle route: [http://tinyurl.com/neversink-gorge](http://tinyurl.com/neversink-gorge)\n\nSince this is a remote gorge (at least by east coast standards) and the hardest sections are the most remote carrying the New York new jersey trail conference neversink gorge trail map (which is at [https://www.nynjtc.org/sites/default/files/NYNJTC\\_NeversinkGorgeMap-2017.pdf](https://www.nynjtc.org/sites/default/files/NYNJTC_NeversinkGorgeMap-2017.pdf) ) would be a good idea.\n\n[**Google Map of New York Whitewater**](https://www.google.com/maps/d/edit?mid=zjdnDE8H0TLg.kJnMWGapL4xk)\n\n[**New York Whitewater Paddlers Facebook Group**](https://www.facebook.com/groups/108070075877312/)","averageGradient":null,"maxGradient":null,"length":"11.4","correlations":[{"reachID":"1356","isPrimary":true,"correlationDetails":{"metric":"cfs","belowRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableRangeComment":null,"mediumRunnableRangeComment":null,"highRunnableRangeComment":null,"aboveRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"highRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"beginLowRunnable":"640","beginMediumRunnable":"750","beginHighRunnable":"2000","endHighRunnable":"5000"},"gaugeInfo":{"name":"NEVERSINK RIVER AT BRIDGEVILLE NY","gaugeSource":"USGS","gaugeSourceIdentifier":"01436690","gaugeFetchStatus":"ACTIVE","latestFlowReading":{"value":"413","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:30:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"latestStageReading":{"value":"5.55","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:30:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"location":{"latitude":"41.63780556","longitude":"-74.61738889"},"externalSourceLinks":{"sourceLi